  "subtitle": "The machine that learns your brain's language for sound, then writes into your auditory nerve",
  "why_scout_cares": "This is the museum's only output-to-nervous-system prosthetic: a computer that analyzes sound, encodes it, and fires electrical pulse trains directly into the cochlear nerve — the machine becoming a sense organ. Every other clinical device in the collection reads the body (EEG, EMG, GSR); this one writes back into it. It reverses the direction of the machine-human boundary and covers the wholly unexplored auditory prosthetic gap.",
